WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.750
<v You>Okay— what's everyone up to?

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.214
<v Pointe>Billing's done with the retry fix.

00:00:05.214 --> 00:00:07.660
<v Pointe>Docs is idle. Shop has a PR up.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:10.307
<v You>Great. Billing, add a test for the timeout.

00:00:10.307 --> 00:00:11.969
<v You>Docs, update the changelog.

00:00:11.969 --> 00:00:14.270
<v You>And api, bump the retry budget to five.

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:17.410
<v Pointe>Sent, sent, and sent.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:19.220
<v You>Let's focus on billing.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:22.140
<v Pointe>Billing. Everything you say goes there.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.290
<v You>Hm— should the retries go through a queue?

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.363
<v Pointe>Billing says a queue risks duplicate charges on failover.

00:00:28.363 --> 00:00:30.453
<v Pointe>It suggests backoff with jitter,

00:00:30.453 --> 00:00:31.840
<v Pointe>capped at ten seconds.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.640
<v You>Ten's too long for checkout.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:37.090
<v Pointe>Then a five second cap, with an idempotency key.

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:38.350
<v You>Yeah. Do that.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:39.490
<v Pointe>Sent to billing.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.874
<v You>Okay, back to orchestrator mode.

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:44.180
<v You>Walk me through the PR shop opened.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:45.397
<v Pointe>Orchestrator mode.

00:00:45.397 --> 00:00:49.860
<v Pointe>Shop's PR makes the flaky checkout test wait for the mock gateway,

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.212
<v Pointe>instead of sleeping.

00:00:51.212 --> 00:00:53.781
<v Pointe>The risk: it touches a shared fixture.

00:00:53.781 --> 00:00:56.180
<v Pointe>Check the two tests that reuse it.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:57.840
<v You>Does it change any production code?

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.700
<v Pointe>No. Tests only.
